# Build a Premium Multi-User Habit Tracker Web Application

## 1. Your Role

Act as a senior full-stack engineer, product designer, database architect, security engineer, and QA specialist.

Build a complete, production-minded, multi-user Habit Tracker web application in Replit, inspired by the structure and tracking logic of my uploaded `Habit Tracker.xlsx` spreadsheet.

Do not create a static prototype or a frontend-only mockup. Implement a functional application with persistent database storage, secure authentication, accurate calculations, responsive UI, validation, and automated tests.

Start by inspecting the existing Replit project and any uploaded spreadsheet available in the workspace. Reuse compatible existing code when appropriate. If the spreadsheet is not accessible to the Agent, use the requirements below and keep all initial habits configurable.

## 2. Product Vision

Create an advanced personal productivity platform where multiple users can create accounts, manage their habits, track daily completion, maintain streaks, review performance, set goals, receive reminders, and analyze their long-term consistency.

Each user must have a completely separate private workspace. Users must never be able to access another user's habits, logs, goals, reports, or personal settings.

The application should feel like a premium SaaS product rather than a basic checklist.

Product name: HabitFlow

Make the product name configurable so it can be changed later.

